                "Alegria",
                "flat design",
                "geometric style",
                "simplified figures",
                "pastel colors",
                "big tech art",
                "disproportionate limbs"
              ],
              "mood": [],
              "colors": [],
              "palette": null,
              "text": "Corporate Memphis (also known as Alegria, big tech art, or flat art) is a term used, often disparagingly, to describe a flat, geometric art style widely used in illustrations of tech companies in the late 2010s and early 2020s. It is characterised by simplified human figures with disproportionate limbs and bright, often pastel, colours.",
